Despite billions in city and county spending, L.A. hosts the nation's largest unsheltered homeless population. 

@CityJournal reporters asked the simple question that few seem to have asked: Where, exactly, are these people coming from?

New investigation from @christopherrufo and @kennethschrupp: city-journal.org/article/la-…

"Newsom is taking millions of dollars from taxpayers to give tablets to every inmate in California. He doesn't deny that part—that's happening. He just says that the usage is being monitored. Even if it is, which it clearly is not—not well enough, anyway—it's totally outrageous to give tablets to prisoners...

...I don't care if all they're doing is going to Instagram to find fun new recipes...it would still be an outrage that they have a tablet. Prison is not supposed to be fun."

@MattWalshBlo

"The Newsom administration devoted a significant sum of money towards broad-based population prevention. Very few dollars were allocated for the kind of psychiatric residential treatment facilities that could help kids who repeatedly accessed emergency rooms for crisis. 

The result was a total mismatch between what was needed and what was offered to people."

@buttonslives discusses her @CityJournal report about how the equity agenda has consumed California's youth mental health crisis: city-jo
